# Built frontend bundles are generated by esbuild (LF). Pin to LF so the
# frontend bundle-drift CI gate is deterministic across Windows/Linux.
*.bundle.js text eol=lf
*.bundle.js.map text eol=lf

# Source that FEEDS those bundles must be pinned too, or the output is not
# actually deterministic. esbuild embeds the raw source text — line endings and
# all — in each map's `sourcesContent`, so a map built from a CRLF checkout
# differs byte-for-byte from one built from an LF checkout even when the
# emitted .bundle.js is identical. With core.autocrlf=true these are stored LF
# and checked out CRLF, while `health.entry.jsx` had somehow stayed LF on disk
# — so a rebuild churned its map on every frontend PR, and the drift gate could
# not see it because that gate diffs *.bundle.js and *.html only.
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# ...and the plain .js that get BUNDLED. `session-guard.js` is imported by
# every entry, so it lands in `sourcesContent` of every map; it was CRLF on
# Windows and LF on a Linux runner, which made the maps differ and failed the
# (now working) drift gate on the v2.7.17 tag. Scoped to home-hifi/ on purpose:
# __tests__/*.js are never bundled, and v1/vendor/react*.min.js is a vendored
# artefact better left byte-for-byte as shipped.
src/subarr/static/v1/home-hifi/*.js text eol=lf
src/subarr/static/v1/**/*.html text eol=lf

# Every shell script here is executed on Linux: docker-entrypoint.sh is COPYd
# into the image, deploy/scripts/install.sh is run by users, the rest are
# dev/ops helpers run under WSL. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites them to CRLF, which turns the shebang into `#!/bin/sh\r` and makes
# the kernel look for an interpreter that does not exist. The image then dies
# with `exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory`,
# naming the script rather than the cause. CI checks out LF so it never sees
# this; only local builds break. Same reasoning as the .githooks pin below.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Git hooks are POSIX sh — pin to LF so a CRLF shebang (#!/bin/sh\r) can't
# break execution on Linux/macOS (incl. CI clones).
.githooks/* text eol=lf
